      "content": "This transition to fixed-timer smart lights is likely to create a more consistent traffic flow, as the predictability will improve through predefined timing and route patterns. However, it will depend on the efficiency of these fixed-timers and the crafting of the loops. In the short term, there might be an initial dip in optimization and potentially slower throughput as the new system learns and adapts. But in the long run, a stable traffic pattern could reduce congestion, particularly in peak hours. Careful monitoring and adjustments to the fixed-timer settings may be necessary to maintain or improve throughput levels. It's also important to closely monitor the behavioral response of drivers as they adapt to the new traffic patterns. In-depth analysis of traffic data post-implementation will be essential to ensure the expected advantages in throughput are realized.",
