      "role": "user",
      "content": "The planners are leaning towards the \"predictability\" aspect because they're worried about last week's weird routing spike. They think the current adaptive protocols are too reactive and cause too much chaos for emergency services to predict. Given that they want to prioritize that predictability over real-time optimization, do you see any major risks in moving away from the active routing model?",
